<title>USA: US banks free rsrvs $899 mln/day rvd April 9 2 wks. [CORRECTED 20:47 GMT]</title>
<headline>US banks free rsrvs $899 mln/day rvd April 9 2 wks. [CORRECTED 20:47 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had revised free reserves of $899 million per day in the two weeks ended April 9, versus revised free reserves of $888 million in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>(Corrects figure in headline to $899 mln/day from $889 mln/day.)</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $61 million versus $38 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>((-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660))</p>
